---
title: Field Types
name: Field Types
description: How Prisma field types map to form inputs, and how sensitive fields are auto-hidden from list views.
---

sveltekit-admin inspects each field's Prisma type to decide how to render it
in create/edit forms.

## Supported field types

| Prisma Type                     | Form Input                                    |
| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| `String`                          | text input (textarea for `description`/`content`/`body`) |
| `Int`, `Float`, `Decimal`, `BigInt` | number input                                  |
| `Boolean`                          | checkbox                                        |
| `DateTime`                         | datetime-local input                            |
| `Json`                             | textarea with JSON                              |

Relations are handled separately — see [Relations](/docs/relations).

## Automatic hiding of sensitive fields

The admin auto-hides common sensitive fields from **list views**: any field
whose name contains `password`, `hash`, `secret`, or `token`
(case-insensitive). This covers fields like `hashedPassword`,
`passwordHash`, and `refreshToken` without any configuration.

Two things worth knowing about this heuristic:

- **It matches on substrings.** It also catches names you might not expect,
  like `hashtag`, `tokenCount`, or `secretariat`. If the heuristic gets a
  field wrong, list it explicitly in that model's `listFields`
  (see [Model Configuration](/docs/model-configuration)) — that's the
  override, and the only way to show a column the heuristic hides.
- **It only applies to list views.** Edit forms still render these fields
  normally, so you can set or update a value. Use `models[].hidden` if you
  want a field removed from the admin entirely, everywhere.
